====================================================================================================
VERDICT: OUTCOME (b) at the CENTRE -- every member of both functionals on both layers has a finite limit at r -> 0+.
  Layer A (the infalling seat): the normalised excess reads the frame's dihedral angle at the root, orbit
  {phi_3, pi-phi_3, pi-phi_3, phi_3}: FINITE-NONTRIVIAL, real (T1, P1-7a).  The raw CARRY-8 functional reads 0
  for every admissible frame (T1f, P1-7b): the letter of the frozen definition selects a functional with no content.
  Layer C (the hole): the presented vectors sum to zero at the centre (T2a); the (+++) triangle is the hemisphere,
  Omega = 2 pi with half-angle sign -1, the other three 0 (P1-7c).  Horizon: Omega -> 0 both sides (P1-8a).
  INSIDE: at every presented-collision radius (layer A: r* = r_s Delta/(1 - g12^2), T3) two presented directions
  are antipodal for half the orbit and S + iV -> 0: Im Omega -> oo, a LOGARITHMIC singularity with NO rod in a
  denominator (P1-8c, P1-13a).  The rod-free curvature reading is regular at r = 0 and singular at r*.
  Conditional on: KIN-2a, CONT-1 (+i sheet), RULING-2, the principal-branch convention of section 2.
====================================================================================================
COMPARISON STAGE (names spoken here only):
  - Gauss-Bonnet: the excess of the presented triangle is its enclosed curvature integral; the centre value on the
    seat layer is a dihedral angle, finite -- no 1/r^3 tidal divergence is reproduced or expected here.
  - The layer-C hemisphere at the centre (2 pi, half-angle -1) is the spin-lift sign of a full turn: the deck Z2.
  - Interior antipodal collisions at r* have no standard-model analogue claimed; lineage unsearched.
